+/**
+ * Write data to the copy-on-write diff file rather than to the exported
+ * file.
+ *
+ * The data in the diff file is tracked in chunks of DIFFPAGESIZE bytes.
+ * When a page is written to for the first time, it is pre-filled with
+ * the data from the exported file unless the write covers the whole
+ * page, so that the parts of the page which are not overwritten keep
+ * their original content. For a sparse diff file, pages live at the
+ * offset of the page in the export; otherwise, every newly written page
+ * is mapped to the end of the diff file.
+ *
